.TH NBSP 1 "July 20, 2026" "nbsp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nbsp \- a small asynchronous prompt for macOS and Zsh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nbsp init zsh
[
.B --detached
]
.br
.B nbsp prompt
[
.B --status
.I N
]
[
.B --duration-ms
.I N
]
[
.B --jobs
.I N
]
.br
.B nbsp data
[
.B --status
.I N
]
[
.B --duration-ms
.I N
]
[
.B --jobs
.I N
]
[
.B --format
.I lines|nul
]
.br
.B nbsp refresh
[
.B --cwd
.I PATH
]
[
.B --notify
]
[
.B --force
]
.br
.B nbsp cache clear
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nbsp
renders an opinionated one-line Zsh prompt containing a shortened working
directory, Git status, active NVM version, command duration, background job
count, and the exact nonzero exit status. Failures render as a compact red
status joined to the prompt character, such as e1% or e127%.
.PP
The built-in presentation is intentionally fixed. Detached mode exposes the
same cached facts and asynchronous lifecycle for user-owned prompts without
reading or writing
.B PROMPT
or
.BR RPROMPT .
.PP
The foreground renderer never executes Git. It reads the branch directly from
the repository metadata and consumes a small cached status snapshot. A
background refresh obtains porcelain-v2 status and asks ZLE to redraw the
prompt when ready.
.SH SETUP
Add the following after NVM initialization in
.IR ~/.zshrc :
.PP
.EX
eval "$(nbsp init zsh)"
.EE
.PP
To build a custom prompt, use:
.PP
.EX
eval "$(nbsp init zsh --detached)"
.EE
.SH EXTERNAL COMMAND EDITING
If it is not already bound,
.B Alt+E
opens the current Zsh editing buffer in an external editor. Save and quit the
editor to return the edited text to Zsh. The command is not executed until
Enter is pressed, and multiline buffers are supported.
.PP
The editor is selected from
.BR VISUAL ,
then
.BR EDITOR ,
with
.B vi
as the fallback. With vi, vim, or nvim, the Zsh cursor returns to the line and
character where the editor was closed. Other editors, or an invalid cursor
report, place it at the end of the edited command.
.PP
The binding is installed in the Emacs, Vi insert, and Vi command keymaps
without replacing existing user or plugin bindings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init zsh
Print the fixed-prompt Zsh integration code. With
.BR --detached ,
install the data lifecycle without modifying the prompt.
.TP
.B prompt
Render a prompt using supplied command metadata and the current directory.
.TP
.B data
Print the cache-only prompt facts. The default
.B lines
format is a versioned sequence of percent-encoded key=value records.
.B --format nul
prints alternating raw key and value records separated by NUL bytes.
Neither format executes Git.
.TP
.B refresh
Refresh the Git snapshot for a directory. This is normally asynchronous.
The
.B --force
option bypasses only the 250 ms duplicate-refresh debounce; locking, timeout,
and atomic cache publication are unchanged.
.TP
.B cache clear
Remove cache and lock files owned by nbsp.
.SH DETACHED MODE
Detached mode publishes a global Zsh associative array named
.B NBSP_DATA
after each precmd and asynchronous refresh. It also exposes
.B nbsp_data_update_functions
for custom redraw callbacks and
.B nbsp_prompt_escape
for safely embedding dynamic text in Zsh prompts.
.PP
The complete schema, safe parsing rules, and custom prompt examples are
documented in
.IR custom-prompts.md ,
installed under the nobsprompt documentation directory.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Presentation is not configurable in built-in mode. Use detached mode to choose
colors, symbols, layout, segment visibility, or duration thresholds.
.TP
.B NBSP_GIT_TIMEOUT_MS
Background Git timeout in milliseconds. Default: 1500.
.TP
.B NBSP_CACHE_DIR
Override the cache root. The default is the XDG cache directory when set,
otherwise ~/Library/Caches/nbsp.
.SH GIT MARKERS
.B +
staged,
.B ~
modified,
.B ?
untracked,
.B !
conflicted,
.B ^
ahead,
.B v
behind, and
.B *
stashes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 2 for invalid command-line usage, and 1 for operational,
serialization, refresh, or cache failures. Optional prompt context failures do
not prevent a prompt from being rendered.
